  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5802.21 Snap acceleration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5802.21 “Snap acceleration” means the SAE J1667 test procedure and refers to the rapid depression of the accelerator pedal by the vehicle operator in order to reach maximum governed RPM as part of the test.\n\nSource. #6887, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-99",
